\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Retrospective non-inferiority for the F1 residence endpoint at the registered margin of $0.001$ nats. Lower loss is better, so the question is whether the \emph  {upper} bound falls below $+0.001$. It does not, in any of the four comparisons, even under the most permissive procedure (a pointwise one-sided bootstrap percentile with no multiplicity adjustment). This assessment is retrospective and does not replace the registered outcome.}}{6}{table.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:equivalence}{{2}{6}{Retrospective non-inferiority for the F1 residence endpoint at the registered margin of $0.001$ nats. Lower loss is better, so the question is whether the \emph {upper} bound falls below $+0.001$. It does not, in any of the four comparisons, even under the most permissive procedure (a pointwise one-sided bootstrap percentile with no multiplicity adjustment). This assessment is retrospective and does not replace the registered outcome}{table.caption.3}{}}
